# counter harness spec-potential calculate
# force_calls count spec-potential evaluations and are not divided by the image count
# Gaussian-process predictions stay outside the tally
# the mean is round-half-even over successes; a Hessian index other than 1 is a failure
# a start at the wall-clock ceiling is a cap failure and keeps its harness call count
# cycling is a later geometry within 1e-6 of an earlier acquisition
successes 0
nfailed 6
n 6
transition_states 0
code CatLearn
code_version 0.7.0
commit 6a307f32dbef18da9cd848f632d082b8e4f117b1
algorithm ML-NEB
template catlearn/neb-pt-heptamer-default
tuning default
problem neb/Pt-heptamer
counter harness
images 8
wall_limit 7200
partial true
note ML-NEB on the 13 Pt-heptamer pairs with 8 interior images. Linear interpolation, acquisition acq_5, uncertainty convergence 0.05, MDMin dt 0.025, 750 surrogate steps, maximum surrogate step 0.25, improved tangent, automatic spring, and 500 iterations are the library defaults. The surrogate is the library Gaussian kernel with one length scale. The fingerprint is the masked Cartesian coordinates, and the training targets include the gradients. The training set has no size limit. The band width is the problem interior count plus the two endpoints. The library's unset image value is a spacing of 0.25, and each tutorial sets its own integer. The force stop is the problem norm 0.01 eV/Ang. The force-call cap is the problem cap. The library step budget is 500. A start that reaches the wall-clock ceiling of 7200 seconds is a cap failure. The recorded cost is the harness call count at that stop. Cycling is recorded when a later acquisition lies within 1e-6 of an earlier geometry.
